{"schema_version": 4, "name": "s2-ecology-to-proximity", "investigation": "eukaryogenesis", "created": "2026-10-27", "title": "S2 \u2014 Ecology to proximity: when does cross-feeding select for persistent contact?", "phase": "Calibrate", "status": "planned", "design_status": "drafted", "simulation_status": "not_run", "evaluation_status": "not_evaluated", "gate_status": "not_started", "topic": "spatial-ecology", "tags": ["symbiosis", "reaction-diffusion", "agents", "proximity", "selection"], "concept": "Physical association made operational as encounter rate, adhesion lifetime, diffusion length, and spatial crowding. The two cross-feeding lineages (the S1 community) placed proximate (mixed) vs distant (segregated) along the pore, under varying diffusion \u2014 measuring whether the cross-feeding benefit is distance-dependent.", "question": "When do cross-feeding benefits select for persistent proximity rather than independent coexistence? Does the predicted selection for proximity disappear under high diffusion / well-mixed conditions?", "hypothesis": "Below a critical diffusion length the cross-feeding flux is distance-dependent and selects for sustained contact; under well-mixed (high-diffusion) conditions the proximity advantage collapses, so selection for contact is a spatial-structure effect, not a given.", "claim": "Selection may favor sustained contact: in spatially structured (low-diffusion) environments the S1 cross-feeding flux is strongly distance-dependent \u2014 proximate (mixed) partners sustain the exchange while distant (segregated) partners lose it \u2014 creating a precondition for intimate symbiosis. The advantage vanishes under high diffusion (well-mixed), so proximity selection is contingent on spatial structure.", "behavior_tests": [{"name": "proximity-selected-under-finite-diffusion", "classification": "primary", "description": "At low diffusion the proximate (mixed) community sustains cross-lineage metabolite flux that a distant (segregated) community loses \u2014 so the cross-feeding benefit is distance-dependent and selects for contact. The threshold discriminates mixed (proximate) from the segregated control.", "measure": {"kind": "derived_scalar", "path": "settled_cross_lineage_flux"}, "pass_if": {"op": ">", "value": "1e-22", "provenance": {"kind": "calibration", "note": "Calibrated at p_diacid=1e-8, p_monoacid=1e-7, k_wash=0.01, k_diffusion=0.001, 250 steps: mixed (proximate) settles to 4.0e-22 (PASS) while the segregated control (the `distant-control` variant) settles to 1.8e-23 (FAIL) \u2014 a 22x proximity advantage. Under high diffusion (k_diffusion=0.1) the mixed/segregated ratio falls to 1.26: the advantage vanishes well-mixed."}}, "cites": ["radler-nature-2026"]}], "acceptance_criteria": [{"behavior": "proximity-selected-under-finite-diffusion"}], "findings": [{"id": "s2-proximity-distance-dependent-calibrated", "statement": "Calibrated (k_diffusion=0.001, 250 steps): proximate (mixed) partners sustain cross-lineage flux 4.0e-22 mol/tick while distant (segregated) partners sustain only 1.8e-23 \u2014 a 22x proximity advantage, so selection favours persistent contact. The advantage is diffusion- dependent: at k_diffusion=0.1 the mixed/segregated ratio is 1.26 (proximity barely matters, diffusion carries the intermediate). Establishes that proximity selection is a spatial- structure effect, not a given \u2014 a precondition for intimate symbiosis. Direct in-process run.", "evidence": {"from_test": "proximity-selected-under-finite-diffusion", "measure": "settled_cross_lineage_flux", "observed": 4.005e-22, "conditions": {"structure": "proximate"}, "fidelity": "reproduction"}, "provenance": {"kind": "run", "run_date": "2026-10-28", "note": "In-process run of metabolite_exchange_community (250 steps). Proper 2x2 (placement x diffusion): at LOW diffusion (k=0.001) proximate (mixed) settled_cross_lineage_flux 4.005e-22 vs distant (segregated) 1.821e-23 \u2014 a 22x proximity advantage; at HIGH diffusion (k=0.1) the ratio collapses to 1.3x (mixed 4.005e-22, segregated 3.191e-22). Proximity selection is contingent on spatial structure. NOTE: reproduces only at ~250 steps (a 60-step run under-reads the flux by ~17x).", "run_ids": ["viva_genesis.composites.metabolite_exchange_community.metabolite_exchange_community__1793462352__656184"], "model_version": "mv:6405f4ca2bcd6f11"}, "cites": ["radler-nature-2026"], "expected": {"cites": ["radler-nature-2026"]}, "_lifecycle_floor": "provisional-claim"}, {"id": "s2-distant-partners-lose-the-exchange", "statement": "At low diffusion the distant (segregated) partners sustain cross-lineage flux of only 1.821e-23 \u2014 an order of magnitude below the proximate 4.005e-22 (the 22x advantage). Distance breaks the exchange, so persistent contact is selected only where spatial structure holds.", "evidence": {"from_test": "proximity-selected-under-finite-diffusion", "measure": "settled_cross_lineage_flux", "observed": 1.821e-23, "conditions": {"structure": "distant"}, "fidelity": "reproduction"}, "provenance": {"kind": "run", "run_date": "2026-10-28", "note": "Same composite, distant (segregated) placement at low diffusion (k=0.001), 250 steps: settled_cross_lineage_flux 1.821e-23.", "run_ids": ["viva_genesis.composites.metabolite_exchange_community.metabolite_exchange_community__1793462352__656184"], "model_version": "mv:6405f4ca2bcd6f11"}, "cites": ["radler-nature-2026"], "expected": {"cites": ["radler-nature-2026"]}, "_lifecycle_floor": "provisional-claim"}], "literature_anchors": [{"expectation": "Asgard protrusions set the length/time scales of transient contact.", "model_observable": "settled_cross_lineage_flux", "source": "Radler et al. 2026, Nature", "cites": ["radler-nature-2026"], "status_in_workspace": "proposed"}], "parent_studies": [{"study": "s1-metabolic-partnership", "relation": "builds-on"}], "baseline": [{"name": "baseline", "composite": "viva_genesis.composites.metabolite_exchange_community.metabolite_exchange_community", "params": {"lineages": "fixer:4,reducer:4", "coupling": "shared", "model_proto_ecology": "reaction_universe", "p_diacid": 1e-08, "p_monoacid": 1e-07, "k_wash": 0.01, "placement": "mixed", "k_diffusion": 0.001}, "note": "First-fidelity arm: reuses the S1 metabolite-exchange community with placement + diffusion as the proximity lever. settled_cross_lineage_flux (metabolite flux between lineages) is the distance-dependent benefit. The dedicated reaction-diffusion PDE with a continuous separation axis is the next-fidelity arm."}], "variants": [{"name": "distant-control", "base": "baseline", "over": {"placement": "segregated"}}, {"name": "well-mixed-control", "base": "baseline", "over": {"k_diffusion": 0.1}}], "visualizations": [{"name": "proximity-diffusion", "title": "Proximity sustains exchange only where structure holds \u2014 flux vs diffusion (22x \u2192 1.3x)", "address": "html:viz/proximity-diffusion.html", "render": "python -m viva_genesis.viz_endosym proximity-diffusion {chart}", "requires": [], "covers": ["settled_cross_lineage_flux"]}, {"name": "proximity-selects-contact", "address": "local:S2EcologyProximityViz", "config": {"title": "S2 \u2014 proximity selects for contact (cross-lineage flux, proximate vs distant)"}, "rendered": "workspace/studies/s2-ecology-to-proximity/viz/proximity-selects-contact.html"}], "observables": ["exchange/cross_lineage_flux_total"], "data_inputs": [{"name": "Asgard live-cell microscopy (figshare/BioImage)", "use": "protrusion length/time priors", "url": "https://doi.org/10.6084/m9.figshare.30676367"}], "runs": [{"run_id": "viva_genesis.composites.metabolite_exchange_community.metabolite_exchange_community__1793462352__656184", "spec_id": "s2-ecology-to-proximity", "label": "viva_genesis.composites.metabolite_exchange_community.metabolite_exchange_community__1793462352__656184", "sim_name": "viva_genesis.composites.metabolite_exchange_community.metabolite_exchange_community__1793462352__656184", "variant": null, "comp